<p>Open any <a href="/blog/">blog post</a> or demo, scroll part of the way down, and come back here. Every page you left halfway shows up in this list, read straight from your browser's <code>localStorage</code>:</p>
<div class="demo__live-widget reading-list" data-reading-list hidden>
  <p data-reading-list-empty tabindex="-1">No saved positions yet. Nothing is stored until you've scrolled at least 3% into a page, and a page is forgotten again once you reach the end.</p>
  <ul class="demo__live-list" data-reading-list-items></ul>
  <button type="button" class="button" data-reading-list-clear hidden>Forget all saved positions</button>
</div>
<noscript><p>Resume Reading needs JavaScript, which is turned off in your browser.</p></noscript>
<p>Then open one of those pages again from a link. A "Continue reading" box appears at the bottom, offering to take you back to where you were. This page tracks you too: scroll down, leave, and come back.</p>
